      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we also want to do an earlier check along the lines of:\n```\nif ((colorSamples \u003e SampleCount::k1 \u0026\u0026 this-\u003eavoidMSAA()) ||\n    (depthStencilFormat !\u003d TextureFormat::kUnsupported \u0026\u0026 this-\u003eavoidDepthMode()) {\n    return false;\n}\n```\n\nIf we encountered a precompile pipeline that has MSAA or a depth attachment, I think we can ignore them because they fall into 2 cases:\n1. This was a renderer that triggered the use of stencil or msaa so going forward, no one will be able trigger a pipeline cache hit on this pipeline desc even if we just fiddle with the DS attachment.\n2. This desc came from a non-stencil, non-MSAA draw that got looped into a msaa renderpass for some other reason, in which case there\u0027s a very strong chance that the set of precompiled pipelines already includes the single-sampled, non-stencil version.\n\nAll we need here with the final `!this-\u003eavoidDepthMode()` check is to gracefully convert any precompile 1x+D16 render passes into a depth-less render pass.",
